James inquired about literature on simple models of energy systems with battery storage, emphasizing intermittent renewables and energy arbitrage optimization. I recommended key areas of literature, including Energy Systems Optimization, Battery Storage and Energy Arbitrage Models, and integration of renewables. I highlighted the importance of examining energy economics and operations research for foundational methods. In response to a follow-up question, I provided several key papers: notable ones include "Optimal Planning of Renewable Energy Systems with Storage," focusing on cost efficiency; "Battery Energy Storage System: A Review of Control Strategies and Applications," exploring various control strategies; and "Optimal Operation of a Battery Energy Storage System for Energy Arbitrage in Smart Grids," which develops a model for optimizing battery operations. These sources were intended to deepen his understanding of the subject matter.
